//@ known-failure: MODE-DEPENDENT BY DESIGN. Without SOUNIO_EFFECT_INFER=1 this file reports E035
//@ known-failure: and does not compile — which is the CORRECT shipped behaviour, since the
//@ known-failure: intermediate functions mutate through an exclusive reference without declaring
//@ known-failure: Mut. It is a known-failure and not a run-pass for exactly that reason: a
//@ known-failure: run-pass whose verdict depends on an environment variable is a test that passes
//@ known-failure: or fails depending on how it is invoked, the same defect that put
//@ known-failure: incomplete_assignment_at_eof.sio in tests/compile-fail and broke CI.
//@ known-failure:
//@ known-failure: Run it deliberately, with the flag, to see the design under test:
//@ known-failure:   SOUNIO_EFFECT_INFER=1 SOUNIO_EFFECT_INFER_TRACE=1 <madaros> --check <this file>
//@ known-failure: exactly ONE W045 must appear, on pub_top and not on priv_mid.


// The boundary half of §7.2.1: inference is SILENT inside a module and VISIBLE at its edge.
//
//   SOUNIO_EFFECT_INFER=1 SOUNIO_EFFECT_INFER_TRACE=1 <madaros> --check <this file>
//
// must print exactly ONE warning, and the trace must show both propagations:
//   effect_infer: priv_mid += Mut (from leaf)     <- private: infers, stays silent
//   warning[W045]                                  <- only here
//   effect_infer: pub_top  += Mut (from priv_mid)  <- pub: infers AND warns
//
// One warning and not two is the whole contract. `priv_mid` inferring quietly is the point of
// inference — the author does not reason about effects internally. `pub_top` warns because outside
// the module the declaration is all a caller can read, so that is where the annotation earns its
// keep.
//
// Controls, all measured: with the flag off there are zero W045 and the E035 returns (shipped
// semantics unchanged); a pub fn that already declares the effect produces zero W045.

struct S {
    v: i64,
}

fn leaf(s: &!S) with Mut {
    (*s).v = 1
}

fn priv_mid(s: &!S) {
    leaf(s)
}

pub fn pub_top(s: &!S) {
    priv_mid(s)
}

fn main() with IO, Mut, Panic, Div {
    var x = S { v: 0 }
    pub_top(&!x)
    print_int(x.v)
    println(" boundary")
}
